From: a1go3 <116062404+a1go3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:54:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tray): open the window below the macOS menu bar icon on
 a left click

A left click on the status item now hangs the main window below the icon, like a menu bar popover, and the app hides it again when it deactivates; a right click or Control-click opens the tray menu as before. The window keeps its size, opens on the active Space without adding a Dock icon, and returns to its previous place on the next regular show.

Changelog: macOS: clicking the menu bar icon opens the main window below it; right-click opens the menu
